## English License & Attribution Terms

### 1. Original Research Dossiers, Forensic Reports & Analytical Tables (`research/*.md`, `research/zh-cn/*.md`, `evidence/evidence-report.md`, `evidence/zh-cn/evidence-report.md`, `antigravity-256k-report.md`, `index.html`)

All original investigative prose, static disassembly write-ups, local SQLite database statistical aggregations, and comparison tables authored in this repository are licensed under **[Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)**.

You are free to share (copy, redistribute) and adapt (translate, quote, remix) this original material for any purpose (including journalism, academic research, and technical analysis), **provided that you give appropriate credit by linking to EITHER**:

- **Option A (Repository Citation)**: Clearly attribute the source and provide the full link to this GitHub repository (`https://github.com/magiccodelab/antigravity-256k-context-discrepancy`), OR
- **Option B (Blog Citation)**: Clearly attribute the source and provide the link to the author's original blog post (`https://afengblog.com/blog/antigravity-256k-context-discrepancy.html`).

### 2. Third-Party Raw Snapshots (`evidence/raw/`) & Verbatim Quotes — Fair Use Disclaimer

- **No Binary Redistribution**: This repository is a text and JSON archive. It **does not host or redistribute** any proprietary Google binary executables or installers (`language_server.exe`, `Antigravity-x64.exe`, `cli_linux_x64.tar.gz`). All official binary artifacts analyzed in the reports are referenced strictly via their official Google Cloud Storage (`storage.googleapis.com/antigravity-public`) download URLs and SHA-256 / SHA-512 cryptographic hashes in Sections 1 and 9 of the forensic report for independent verification.
- **Fair Use & Rights Reservation**: The release manifest (`manifest_linux_amd64.json`), the 21 GitHub API JSON snapshots and the forum thread snapshot in `evidence/raw/`, and all verbatim quotes from community threads, the *Additional Terms of Service (ToS)*, and the *Official FAQ* remain the property of their respective copyright holders (including Google LLC and respective GitHub / forum community contributors). They are archived and reproduced here strictly for technical interoperability analysis, security forensics, and public-interest documentation under **Fair Use (17 U.S.C. § 107)**, and are **excluded** from the CC BY 4.0 license above.
- **Third-Party Scripts Not Redistributed**: The official install script (`https://antigravity.google/cli/install.sh`) is referenced by URL and SHA-256 (`62966c07365423bd4dc209355060744058fb30d60f5323e2d360e39de64e5042`) only. The community patch script `patch_agy.py` is not reproduced either; `evidence/raw/gist.json` records only its metadata and SHA-256, and the script remains under the copyright of its author [`@LiraNuna`](https://gist.github.com/LiraNuna/4c058aed3f636f5193f920f64284ff26).
- **Rights Holder Requests**: If you hold rights in any material reproduced here and believe its use goes beyond fair use, please open an issue in this repository identifying the file and passage; it will be reviewed and, where appropriate, removed or reduced to a citation.

